Z||000000||JohnF||11-19-2001||09:03 AM||||On my '88 coupe, to the right (looking forward from driver's seat) of the spare tire, left of the jack and below the tire tool mounting area, there is a clip riveted in place using two rivets.  Clip is about 1.5 inches square.<P>I've owned this car since new and this is the first time I've noticed this hardware.<P>Anyone know what is this for?  Am I missing something?<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||11-19-2001||09:11 AM||||There is a clip in that area that goes into the open end of your lug wrench||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||11-19-2001||09:21 AM||||Thanks for trying but, his clip is below that.  <P>The lug wrench fits under the spare in two clips.  This isn't one of them.  This is installed below the right-hand lug wrench clip.<P>BTW - lug wrench clips are black, this one is aluminum (silver).<P>Never a camera around when I need one!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||9
